var e=`# CHAPTER 26 — Joaquim Leal Reis\r
\r
Monday started like any Monday.\r
\r
Jack and Kim met up, went to school and found Nina. Class. The three of them studying seriously, Kim paying attention, Jack faking it, Nina for real.\r
\r
When the bell for the last class rang and the three were putting their things away, the hallway made a different noise.\r
\r
A buzz. People talking low and fast. People running to the window.\r
\r
— Did you guys see who's out there? — A girl next to them, to her friend. — I can't believe he's here. What do you think he wants?\r
\r
— He's much better-looking in person. — Her friend, pressed against the glass. — Do you think he came to challenge someone?\r
\r
Kim and Jack looked at each other.\r
\r
— What are these people talking about? — Jack.\r
\r
— I have no idea. — Nina. — But it looks like there's someone important outside. You think it's a problem for you guys?\r
\r
— I don't think so. — Kim. — We've had a few quiet days. We haven't done anything. It must be something else.\r
\r
They started down the hallway, trying to avoid the crowd gathering at the front door, to take another route to their favorite spot.\r
\r
And then the school loudspeaker crackled.\r
\r
— Attention. Could Mr. Joaquim Leal Reis please come forward? We need to speak urgently with Mr. Joaquim Leal Reis.\r
\r
Kim stopped in the middle of the hallway.\r
\r
He lowered his head.\r
\r
Jack started laughing. Not a laugh. A fit. Leaning against the wall, hand on his stomach, out of breath.\r
\r
Nina looked from one to the other.\r
\r
— Who's Joaquim?\r
\r
Jack couldn't answer. He just pointed at Kim.\r
\r
Nina looked at Kim. Kim had the face of someone who wanted the hallway floor to open and swallow him whole.\r
\r
— Please. — The loudspeaker again. — Mr. Joaquim Leal Reis. Present yourself immediately.\r
\r
Kim quickened his pace.\r
\r
Too late.\r
\r
— IT'S HIM! — Someone from his class. — HE'S JOAQUIM! THERE!\r
\r
Everyone turned.\r
\r
---\r
\r
In the middle of the crowd at the door, a path opened up.\r
\r
And through it came a young man.\r
\r
Asian features, narrow eyes. Blond hair, long, almost to his shoulders. A white hoodie with black details on the zipper and pockets. White jeans. He walked with his hands in his pockets, slowly, with the air of someone who's used to being looked at everywhere he goes and stopped caring about it a long time ago.\r
\r
Behind him, a quiet young man carrying a padded bag.\r
\r
The blond young man stopped in front of Kim. He took one hand out of his pocket.\r
\r
— Hello. You must be Kim. The guy who impressed me. — A calm voice, with a slight accent. — I'm Shuntaro Chirasu. Rank nine hundred and ninety-eight in the Illusion Fight world ranking. It's a pleasure to meet you.\r
\r
He gave a bow. Short, natural, the way they do in his country. And held out his hand.\r
\r
Kim looked at Jack. Looked at Nina. He wasn't understanding anything. But he shook the hand.\r
\r
Shuntaro smiled.\r
\r
— I came from very far away. From Azuma. Just to fight you. It was nine hours of travel, and I'm very eager for this fight. — Pause. — Would you give me that honor, Mr. Joaquim?\r
\r
Jack had another fit.\r
\r
---\r
\r
Kim shrugged.\r
\r
It had been a few days since the Thunderbolt fight. He turned to the two of them.\r
\r
— So? What do you guys think? I'm not really understanding what's happening. But it looks like this guy wants to fight. And you know I don't run from a fight.\r
\r
Nina had her phone in her hand, screen facing her, and her face changed.\r
\r
— Kim. I don't know if it's a good idea. — Low. — I think you should fight people a little above you. Not way above. This guy is famous. I lived in Azuma for four years. Over there he's like... like a celebrity. He's been in LDI for six months. Six. And he's already in the top thousand in the world. He knows exactly what he's doing. That's my opinion.\r
\r
Jack, recovered, wiped his eye.\r
\r
— Nina. If you want to convince Kim not to fight, that's the worst possible strategy. Telling him the guy is super strong, super famous, super dangerous only makes him want it more. — He looked at Kim. — What I can tell you, Kim, is that the chances of you taking the biggest beating of your life are high. But I don't decide for you. If you want to get beat up, go. The guy is good.\r
\r
Kim looked at Shuntaro.\r
\r
He read his face. His posture. The way he held his shoulders. There was respect there. It wasn't provocation. And there was also the calm certainty of someone who knows he's stronger and doesn't need to say it.\r
\r
— Call me Kim. — Kim. — And another thing. You came from very far away expecting to get something. I don't think you're dumb enough to spend nine hours traveling to challenge just anyone. If you think it's worth fighting me, then let's fight.\r
\r
Shuntaro smiled for real for the first time.\r
\r
The hallway exploded.\r
\r
No one at that school had ever seen a live LDI fight from someone in the top thousand. Phones going up everywhere. People running to tell others.\r
\r
---\r
\r
Right there, in front of the school, the crowd opened a circle.\r
\r
Shuntaro called his assistant, who opened the padded bag and took out two SBIs. One of them was clearly on another level. You could see it in the finish, the weight, the light running along the edge.\r
\r
Kim sat on the ground leaning against the school wall and took his out of his backpack. Jack and Nina helped him get it on.\r
\r
— Be careful. — Nina, adjusting the strap. — He uses his power load very well. Great technique. He's a strategist. He'll analyze you a lot before doing anything. If you can end it fast, end it. Don't let the fight drag on. The truth is your chances of winning are small. Given how much you've trained.\r
\r
— Relax, girl. — Kim. — Don't worry. If I lose, I lost. What can you do. The fun is in trying. From what you guys are saying, he's way stronger than me. If I win, I move up some positions in the ranking. — Pause. — And besides Freddy's bet, this game hasn't paid me a cent yet. Maybe if I climb, I'll start earning something. In the end that's what matters, right?\r
\r
— You're absolutely right, man. — Jack. — Until you're making your bread and egg, it's not worth it. So let's go get that bread and egg.\r
\r
Jack sat down next to Kim with his own SBI in his hand. Nina sat on the other side.\r
\r
— We're going to watch from inside. — Jack.\r
\r
---\r
\r
On the other side of the circle, Shuntaro was already seated, SBI in hand, assistant at his side.\r
\r
He looked at Kim over the crowd.\r
\r
— I hope we have a good fight. — Shuntaro. — But I didn't come this far to lose. Get ready.\r
\r
— There's no reason for me to start a fight if it isn't to win. — Kim. — I don't get into fights to lose.\r
\r
Shuntaro nodded. Satisfied.\r
\r
The two fitted their SBIs at the same time.\r
\r
And the front of Elite Academy, full of people, stood watching two boys sitting on the ground, eyes closed, not moving.\r
`;export{e as default};
